\ collapse-array.8th -- Thinking 8th, Chapter 7
\ Verified with: 8th code/ch07/collapse-array.8th
\
\ 8th's own documentation gives almost exactly Brodie's warning against
\ pick/roll: if you need that many stack positions, the values belong
\ in an array instead. a:close is the direct way to make one, from
\ items already on the stack.

10 20 30 40 4 a:close . cr    \ => [10,20,30,40]

bye
